    <p>
      The final examination period is December 7 <ndash/> 11. The Registrar's
      Office schedules the final exam; the date and time for each section will be
      announced in Camino as soon as they are available.
    </p>

  
  </introduction>

  <subsection xml:id="exam-topics">
    <title>Tentative List of Topics for the Exams</title>

    <p>
      The lists below are <alert>tentative</alert>. They show the topics I
      expect each midterm exam to cover, and I will confirm the exact coverage
      in class before each exam. Every topic links to its section in the
      skeletal notes, and each list matches the review problem set for that
      exam: the leftover problems on those topics, collected for review.
    </p>

    <p>
      <em>Exam #1</em> (Friday, October 9) <mdash/> see
      <url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/M13-Skeletal-Notes/worksheet-review-problems-1.html">Review Problems #1</url>:
    </p>

    <p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/M13-Skeletal-Notes/skel-chapter-hyperbolic-functions.html">Hyperbolic Functions</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/M13-Skeletal-Notes/sec-skel-series-infinite.html">Infinite Series</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/M13-Skeletal-Notes/sec-skel-series-taylor.html">Taylor and Maclaurin Series</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/M13-Skeletal-Notes/sec-skel-series-taylor-convergence.html">Taylor Series and Its Convergence</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/M13-Skeletal-Notes/sec-skel-series-binomial.html">The Binomial Series and Applications of Taylor Series</url></p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </p>

    <p>
      <em>Exam #2</em> (Friday, October 30) <mdash/> see
      <url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/M13-Skeletal-Notes/worksheet-review-problems-2.html">Review Problems #2</url>:
    </p>

    <p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/M13-Skeletal-Notes/sec-skel-geom-3d-coordinates.html">Three-Dimensional Coordinate Systems</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/M13-Skeletal-Notes/sec-skel-geom-vectors.html">Vectors</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/M13-Skeletal-Notes/sec-skel-geom-dot-product.html">The Dot Product</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/M13-Skeletal-Notes/sec-skel-geom-cross-product.html">The Cross Product</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/M13-Skeletal-Notes/sec-skel-geom-parametrization.html">Parametrization of Plane Curves</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/M13-Skeletal-Notes/sec-skel-geom-lines-planes.html">Lines and Planes in Space</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/M13-Skeletal-Notes/sec-skel-geom-conics.html">Conic Sections</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/M13-Skeletal-Notes/sec-skel-geom-quadric-surfaces.html">Quadric Surfaces</url></p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </p>

    <p>
      <em>Exam #3</em> (Friday, November 20) <mdash/> see
      <url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/M13-Skeletal-Notes/worksheet-review-problems-3.html">Review Problems #3</url>:
    </p>

    <p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/M13-Skeletal-Notes/sec-skel-fmv-functions.html">Functions of Several Variables</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/M13-Skeletal-Notes/sec-skel-fmv-limits.html">Limits and Continuity in Higher Dimensions</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/M13-Skeletal-Notes/sec-skel-fmv-partial-derivatives.html">Partial Derivatives</url></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><url href="https://mahmadi-ops.github.io/M13-Skeletal-Notes/sec-skel-fmv-chain-rule.html">The Chain Rule</url></p>
